Z||000000||johnt671||08-07-2001||07:55 PM||||I'm getting a code 24 an my 84 SE.  Haynes said to ignore it if it was set when the car isn't moving, but the way mine acts makes me think this is wrong.  If I start the car up and drive the idle will not drop to the lower speed unless I stop at a light and sit.  It will idle at 1200 or so then set the check engine lifht and as soon as it does that, the idle drops.  When the car is driven the light goes out and stays out.  I did have the tps off last week, and the Haynes book said something about adjust the tps but has no info on this.  Any ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-07-2001||08:36 PM||||well code 24 is vehichle speed sensor.you may want to check that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-07-2001||11:26 PM||||If the speedometer is working the actual VSS is ok. That doesn't mean the ECM is seeing it tho. The buffer in the dash, the ECM, or the wire in between them could have a problem. If you have cruise it may have issues as well.<P>Clear the codes from the ECM and go for a drive. see if the code resets. it may take a few miles before it happens.<P>If this happend only after replacing the TPS, then the TPS is probably part of the problem. The little arm gets bent. I don't have that info handy right now.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||1
